    "FUNC.STANDARDIZE"
  ],
  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "STANDARDIZE computes binary64 (x - mean) / stdev, rejects overflow in x - mean with #NUM!, and flushes subnormals to +0",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, STANDARDIZE(x, mean, standard_dev) rejects standard_dev <= 0 with #NUM!, evaluates difference = x - mean and quotient = difference / standard_dev in binary64 (returning #NUM! if either overflows), and flushes subnormal quotients to +0.0 (so STANDARDIZE(DBL_MIN, 0, 8.684494350556545) = 0). All 10,310 full-bank STANDARDIZE rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0 build 20430 (10,310/10,310 full-bank and 120/120 pinned STANDARDIZE rows) and 16.0.20527.20088 in prefix_metadata (row 210).",
